proof.text:
The support is open and closed in each stratum. Fix $k$, put $I^+=\{i\in I_k: M_{k,i}
eq0\}$, $I^0=\{i\in I_k:M_{k,i}=0\}$, $V^+= igcup_{i\in I^+}t_{k,i}(U_{k,i})$ and $V^0= igcup_{i\in I^0}t_{k,i}(U_{k,i})$. Let $z\in Z_k$ with a geometric point $ ar z$ over $z$, and let $i\in I_k$ with $z\in t_{k,i}(U_{k,i})$. By [lem-weil-pbc-etale-cover-geometric-point-lift] (its second clause, applied to $t_{k,i}$ and a point of $U_{k,i}$ over $z$) there is a geometric point $ ar u$ of $U_{k,i}$ with $t_{k,i}\circ ar u= ar z$, so $ ar z$ factors through $U_{k,i}$, and by [lem-weil-pbc-finite-locally-constant-module-values] (the clause 'moreover', for the sheaf $\iota_k^{-1}\mathcal G$ and its covering of type (1)) $(\iota_k^{-1}\mathcal G)_{ ar z}\cong M_{k,i}$. With step 3: $\iota_k(z)\in\operatorname{Supp}(\mathcal G)$ if and only if $M_{k,i}
eq0$, for every $i$ with $z\in t_{k,i}(U_{k,i})$. Since the covering is jointly surjective, $V^+\cup V^0=Z_k$, the two are disjoint (a point in both would have $M_{k,i}
eq0$ and $M_{k,i'}=0$ for $i,i'$ both computing the same condition), and $V^+=\iota_k^{-1}(\operatorname{Supp}(\mathcal G))$. Both are unions of images of etale morphisms, hence open in $Z_k$ by [lem-weil-pbc-etale-morphism-open-map]. So $V^+$ is open and closed in $Z_k$, and by step 2 ($\iota_k$ a homeomorphism onto $X_k$) $S_k:=\operatorname{Supp}(\mathcal G)\cap X_k=\iota_k(V^+)$ is open and closed in the subspace $X_k$.
